Z||000004||GoCartGuy||03-12-2001||12:01 AM||||Danny,<P>I've the the cooling fan on mine wired to a toggle switch so I can control when its on, easier for those chilly WV winters when you want it to warm up faster.  Anyways, mine runs about 140 with the fan on, even in 95 degree FL heat this summer.  Doesn't seem to hurt the engine.  Anyways, to answer all the upcoming question yet I've got the 195 degree temperatue gauge, and no, no AC.  Kinda rough in FL without it, but that's what the big windows and big engine are for.<P>------------------<BR>'85 GT "The GoCart"||||reg||1
